{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"freezing-smooth-godwit","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## The defect\n\nBug `2c4b-3cd9-8bb0-4493` (velvet-prebeloved-discus) proved a defect class: a function whose\nDEFAULT ARGUMENT is a name imported at module level freezes that binding at import time, so a\ntest that patches the symbol on its DEFINING module only reaches the consumer when the consumer\nhappens not to have been imported yet. Ticket `5ea3-76e5-480a-4464` already ruled this construct\na defect and established the remedy — a named call-time indirection (`_retry_sleep`, and\n`acli_subprocess._backoff_sleep`) — documented in the `_retry_sleep` docstring at\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py:44-58`.\n\nA construct sweep run during `2c4b` found the 5ea3 remediation did NOT convert every site. These\nare LATENT (no test trips them today because every current call site injects the dependency\nexplicitly), so they are filed rather than fixed inside a bug fix's authorisation:\n\n* `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:558` — `steal(..., sleep_fn=time.sleep)`\n* `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py:161` — `steal_pass_lock(..., sleep_fn=time.sleep)`\n* `src/rebar/metrics/analyzers/_jscpd.py:18` — `run: Runner = subprocess.run`\n\nWhy they matter despite being latent: the suite contains GLOBAL `time.sleep` and\n`subprocess.run` patches that these frozen defaults would silently escape — notably the\nrepo-isolation guard at `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py:184`, whose `fail_sleep` exists\nto fail loudly if anything sleeps. A real sleep reached through a frozen default slips past it.\nThe moment any caller stops injecting explicitly, each becomes the `2c4b` bug again.\n\nOut of scope for `2c4b`: that bug fix is authorised to restore the invariant at the seam it\nproved (`access_check.py`), not to refactor three unrelated modules.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each of the three sites resolves its dependency at CALL time, mirroring the established\n      `_retry_sleep` / `_backoff_sleep` indirection, with production behaviour byte-identical.\n- [ ] An explicitly passed `sleep_fn=` / `run=` still wins over the seam.\n- [ ] A test proves the seam is reachable: patch the symbol on its defining module AFTER the\n      consumer module is resident in `sys.modules`, and observe the patch take effect.\n- [ ] No new dependency, no behaviour widening, no weakened test.","id":"9118-3f70-9a0b-454e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Three call-time-seam sites missed by the 5ea3 frozen-default remediation"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787314487568363001,"uuid":"854940d3-e12f-416d-989f-9614e8490ee0"}